    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup centered on elite matchups against back-end rotation arms. **Kyle Tucker** (77.80) headlines our offensive attack; he faces McCullers Jr. in a setup that maximizes his production profile, buoyed by an 18% boost from the opposing starter's xERA. **Gunnar Henderson** (74.77) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) are our next most efficient options. **Gunnar Henderson** remains a priority start due to his favorable dynamic platoon advantage and a base-stealing opportunity against a slow-working starter, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on a high-upside matchup against Bailey Ober, where his 14% platoon boost significantly elevates his output. **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) rounds out our top tier, offering a massive boost from the leadoff spot against Houser, though we remain cautious of the opposing catcher\u2019s 1.86s pop time which slightly dampens his aggressive stolen base floor.\n\nStrategic decisions for today prioritized efficiency over pure power, leading to the exclusion of **Nolan Schanuel** (59.14) from the starting nine. **Nolan Schanuel** was the closest to cracking the lineup, but the optimizer favored the platoon-adjusted ceilings of **Miguel Vargas** and **Andy Pages** against their respective right-handed matchups. We are keeping a close watch on the weather for **Josh Jung** (51.20), who remains benched not only due to a lower score than our active utility players but also due to a 44% rain risk that introduces unnecessary volatility. We are currently proceeding with \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions for **Liam Hicks**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Brady House**; should these confirmed batting orders shuffle downward, we will re-evaluate their dynamic order bonuses to ensure we maintain our competitive edge in the daily Roto standings.",
